  "question": {
    "text": "If $z_1, z_2, z_3 \\in C$ are the vertices of an equilateral triangle, whose centroid is $\\mathrm{z}_0$, then $\\sum_{\\mathrm{k}=1}^3\\left(\\mathrm{z}_{\\mathrm{k}}-\\mathrm{z}_0\\right)^2$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$0$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$1$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "i",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-\\mathrm{i}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{z}_1+\\mathrm{z}_2+\\mathrm{z}_3=3 \\mathrm{z}_0 \\\\ & \\left(\\mathrm{z}_1+\\mathrm{z}_2+\\mathrm{z}_3\\right)^2=9 \\mathrm{z}_0^2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{z}_1^2+\\mathrm{z}_2^2+\\mathrm{z}_3^2+2\\left(\\mathrm{z}_1^2+\\mathrm{z}_2^2+\\mathrm{z}_3^2\\right)=9 \\mathrm{z}_0^2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{z}_1^2+\\mathrm{z}_2^2+\\mathrm{z}_3^2=3 \\mathrm{z}_6^2\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\sum_{\\mathrm{k}=1}^3\\left(\\mathrm{z}_{\\mathrm{k}}-\\mathrm{z}_0\\right)^2=\\left(\\mathrm{z}_1-\\mathrm{z}_0\\right)^2+\\left(\\mathrm{z}_2-\\mathrm{z}_0\\right)^2+\\left(\\mathrm{z}_3-\\mathrm{z}_0\\right)^2 \\\\ & \\quad=\\mathrm{z}_1^2+\\mathrm{z}_2^2+\\mathrm{z}_3^2+3 \\mathrm{z}_0^2-2\\left(\\mathrm{z}_1+\\mathrm{z}_2+\\mathrm{z}_3\\right) \\mathrm{z}_0 \\\\ & =6 \\mathrm{z}_0^2-6 \\mathrm{z}_0^2 \\\\ & =0\\end{aligned}$"
  }
